{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.JucysMurphyCentralElementsQou","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.JucysMurphyCentralElementsQou","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jm_pair_symm_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jm_pair_symm_commute","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L133-L162","doc":"**The key commutation step (proved).** In any ring `A`, let `σ` satisfy\nthe Hecke relation `σ * σ = h • σ + 1` (with `h` a central scalar written\nas `hA`, i.e. `σ * σ = hA * σ + 1` with `hA` commuting with everything), let\n`Jk1 = σ * Jk * σ`, and let `Jk`, `Jk1` commute. Then `σ` commutes with\n`Jk + Jk1` and with `Jk * Jk1`. This is Step 2 of the proof: it is why\nsymmetric polynomials in the multiplicative Jucys–Murphy elements are\ncentral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.level_ell_correction_via_esymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.level_ell_correction_via_esymm","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L113-L130","doc":"Corollary: structural form for the level-ℓ correction to mass.\n\nThe level-ℓ shadow price decomposes as a sum over height-(ℓ+1)\nWedderburn blocks, weighted by the central scalar c_ℓ(λ),\nwhich by Murphy 1992 equals `esymm ℓ (qContent λ)`.  The\nexact closed form (with `[n]_q!` normalisation) is\n*conjectural* and is empirically refuted at ℓ=5 in the\ncompanion remark; the rigorous content is the spectrum\nequality above.  See\n`prop:mass-formula-iterative-lp-dual` for the LP-dual\nstatement and\n`rem:alpha-5-jm-central-empirical-findings` for the\nempirical refutation of the simplest closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jm_central_scalar_eq_esymm_qcontent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jm_central_scalar_eq_esymm_qcontent","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L96-L111","doc":"Murphy 1992: spectrum equation for e_ℓ(J_1,…,J_n) on V_λ.\n\nSubstantive content: the central scalar by which the\nJucys–Murphy elementary symmetric polynomial acts on the\nWedderburn block V_λ equals `esymm ℓ (qContent λ)`.  This is\nNOT a tautology: it states a non-trivial equality between\n`centralScalar` (an opaque field defined by the algebra\naction) and an external `esymm` expression in the q-content\nlist.  Discharged by `spectrum_theorem`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jm_esymm_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jm_esymm_central","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L89-L94","doc":"Step 2: The symmetric polynomials in J_k are central. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou","label":"prop:jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jm_elements_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jm_elements_commute","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L82-L87","doc":"Step 1: The Jucys-Murphy elements pairwise commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.cellContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.cellContent","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L79-L80","doc":"Cell content c(□) = j − i for cell (i, j). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.spectrum_theorem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.spectrum_theorem","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Murphy 1992 spectrum theorem (axiomatised).\nThe central-scalar action of `P_ℓ = e_ℓ(J_1, …, J_n)` on\nthe Wedderburn block `V_λ` equals `e_ℓ` applied to the\nq-content multiset of `λ`.  This is the substantive\ncontent of the structure: NOT a tautology.  Downstream\nconsumers can use this equation to compute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.centralScalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.centralScalar","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Wedderburn-block scalar action of e_ℓ(J_1,…,J_n) on V_λ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.esymmJM_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.esymmJM_central","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The symmetric polynomials in J_k are central. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.jm_commutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.jm_commutes","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The Jucys-Murphy elements pairwise commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.esymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.esymm","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Abstract `e_k` over a List R — the elementary symmetric\npolynomial of degree k in the list's entries.  Plugged in by\ndownstream instances (Mathlib `MvPolynomial.esymm` or\nhand-rolled). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.qContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.qContent","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The q-content multiset of a partition λ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.esymmJM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.esymmJM","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The elementary symmetric polynomial `e_ℓ(J_1,…,J_n)` evaluated in\nthe algebra — an abstract element whose centrality is asserted in\n`jm_esymm_central` below (full Hecke construction pending). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.jm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.jm","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Jucys–Murphy elements J_1, …, J_n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.ring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.ring","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The algebra carries a ring structure (the Iwahori–Hecke algebra\n`H_n(q)`); needed for the multiplicative statements below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.algebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.algebra","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The algebra (placeholder; full Hecke algebra is on\nqou:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAlgebra). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJMSpectrum","kind":"structure","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean#L34-L75","doc":"A Hecke algebra together with its Jucys–Murphy spectrum data.\n\nThe structure is parameterised by an ABSTRACT elementary-\nsymmetric function `e_k : List R → R` to allow downstream\ninstances to plug in either Mathlib's `MvPolynomial.esymm` or\na hand-rolled implementation; we make no assumption about\nits definition here other than that it exists. ","signatureChunk":0}]}